# complex phasor under exp(+j w t), written as its real then imaginary part.
#
# Phi is EXACT at every node, including the mid-edge ones: it lives in a P2
# space and a midpoint carries a genuine solved unknown. A, B, H and E have
# no mid-edge freedom, so at a midpoint they are the mean of the two
# endpoints. docs/FIELD_POSTPROCESSING.md Sec. 8.
#
# WHAT MAY BE READ FROM THIS FILE. The discrete system is exactly gauge
# invariant, and the tree-cotree gauge picks one representative, so Phi and A
# are gauge DEPENDENT -- a different spanning tree shifts Phi by -j*w*psi,
# almost purely imaginary. B, H and E are not. Sec. 9.
#
# iface = 1 means the node's incident tets span more than one body. The nodal
# average straddles a material interface there and E and H are MEANINGLESS:
# E's normal component genuinely jumps across it. Filter on this column.
# Sec. 12. The per-cell arrays in the .vtk have no interface to straddle.
